                  "explanation": "In cardiac surgery, **BIMA** = **Bilateral Internal Mammary Arteries** — both internal mammary arteries (now called internal thoracic arteries) used as bypass conduits, considered superior to saphenous vein grafts for long-term patency. **CTICU** = **Cardiothoracic Intensive Care Unit** — the specialized ICU where heart surgery patients recover. Other abbreviations in the passage: **CABG x3** = 3-vessel bypass, **LAD** = Left Anterior Descending coronary, **Cx** = Circumflex coronary, **EBL** = Estimated Blood Loss, **IABP** = Intra-Aortic Balloon Pump (cardiac assist device), **POD** = Post-Operative Day. None of the distractor expansions exist as medical abbreviations.",
